# Developing SAFT plugins – context for agents and developers

This folder describes one SAFT installation for building a plugin: rules, the plugin API and the business tables.
SAFT is a metadata-driven database application (Laravel, Filament, Livewire). Business tables are defined in the
table designer at runtime; plugins add pages, rules and functions on top – without changing SAFT's core.

## Files

| File | Content |
|---|---|
| `AGENTS.md` | this file: rules, environment, workflow |
| `api-reference.md` | every guaranteed class and method of the plugin API (signatures are authoritative) |
| `schema.md` | the business tables with fields, types, values, relations, formulas and rules |
| `schema.json` | the same, exact – create the tables in tests with `$this->createTablesFromSchema(__DIR__.'/../context/schema.json')` |

Full guide: `docs/manual/DEVELOPER_GUIDE.md` in the SAFT repository. Complete examples: `plugins/lager-umbuchung`
(page, listeners, row action, dashboard widget, tests) and `plugins/ch-pruefungen` (validation rules, formula function).

